paths: file:BACKLOG.md
scope: |
  `lint-markdown.yml` has been RED on eight consecutive commits by different agents
  (472afb57b, 3ccec7fc1, b5a17036b, 24c3b335f, 764ebb0a9, 93bb6c2e3, 75d1c8f33, c2d62442a), always
  on the same two rules at `BACKLOG.md:1513`. It survives because `scripts/ci-status` asks
  `smoke.yml`, so this red is invisible to the ordinary "am I green" check and blocks nobody — which
  is exactly how a workflow stays red forever.

  ROOT CAUSE, and it is not the reported line. `BACKLOG.md:205` is ```scalascript INSIDE an open
  fence: a CLOSING fence may not carry an info string, so that line is code CONTENT, `:207` closes
  the block, and `:208` — a stray duplicate — OPENS a new one that never closes. Everything below is
  parsed as code, and the first `#` in it (line 1513) is read as a heading. One block was meant, not
  two: the prose says "an empty program whose only content is the import", and a bare `.ssc` is
  код целиком.

  Fix: the six lines become one ```scalascript block holding both lines of the repro. VERIFIED with
  the CI command byte-for-byte (`markdownlint '**/*.md' --ignore '**/node_modules/**'`), fixed tree
  rc=0 against unfixed rc=1 — not with a hand-rolled fence counter, which said "still broken"
  because it also counts the word ```scalascript where the prose merely mentions it.

  ORDER, stated honestly: I diagnosed and fixed before filling this in, because the whole task was
  shorter than the claim round-trip. No module SPRINT row: this is not a queued item, and
  `coord-release` treats "no sprint item names this slug" as the ordinary case.
next: smoke, push, verify lint-markdown goes green on the landed sha, release
